  "analysis": "Wow, this is a textbook UAC bypass using fodhelper, followed by execution of a PowerShell empire/cobalt strike payload from HKCU:\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows Update. \n\nLet's trace this:\n\n1. `evt-00305` and `evt-00351`: `whoami.exe /groups` run by `CORP\\m.ward` from PowerShell. Wait, `evt-00501` and `evt-00526` are the Sysmon/Security equivalent events.\n2. `evt-00437` and `evt-00858`: `fodhelper.exe` run by `CORP\\m.ward` from PowerShell (Security & Sysmon).\n3. `evt-00445`, `evt-00478` (and corresponding Sysmon equivalents `evt-00554`, `evt-00564`, `evt-00704`): `svchost.exe` and `consent.exe` - wait, `consent.exe` is launched because of the UAC bypass attempt, or ordinary behavior. But let's look closer.\n4. `evt-01020` and `evt-01186`: `powershell.exe -NoP -NonI -W Hidden -c $x=$((gp HKCU:Software\Microsoft\Windows Update).Update); powershell -NoP -NonI -W Hidden -enc $x`\nThis is a classic payload stored in the registry under `HKCU:Software\\Microsoft\\Windows Update` property `Update` and executed.\n5. `evt-01614` is a very long encoded PowerShell command: `powershell.exe -NoP -NonI -W Hidden -enc SQBGACgAJAB...` (which starts with `IF($PSVERSION...` and disables Script Block Logging!)\nWait, where does this registry property get set? It must have been set in the registry! Registry event codes are 12, 13, 14 in Sysmon. Let's inspect event codes 12 and 13 (Registry Object Added/Deleted, Value Set).\nLet's query the database for registry modifications or any processes before 00:00:26.",
  "plan": "I will inspect registry changes (event_code 12, 13, 14) and any script block logs or network connections (event_code 3) around these times.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sqlite3 /root/data/eventlogs.db \"SELECT event_id, event_code, timestamp, host, user, target_object, details FROM events WHERE event_code IN (12, 13, 14) AND (target_object LIKE '%Windows Update%' OR target_object LIKE '%fodhelper%' OR target_object LIKE '%ms-settings%');\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sqlite3 /root/data/eventlogs.db \"SELECT event_id, event_code, timestamp, host, user, message FROM events WHERE event_id IN ('evt-01537', 'evt-01896');\"\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}
